@crew calder
// SW5, the endgame pool (plans/ending-spec.html section 9): said only after you choose to stay. Every line is
// gated by the bare condition "endgame" (EN2 adds it to the line filter, section 22); "endgame:early" marks the
// lines that only make sense in the first two weeks after you stay (RV21).

== greet
? endgame time:morning
- {hi}. Board's at fourteen. Ordinary day. Good.

== chat
? endgame:early
- You stayed. Good. Training someone new takes a year. I'd rather not.   #funny
? endgame
- No more exams. There are still serial numbers. Learn them.   #funny
- The board doesn't care about rank. Neither do I. Pick a job.
- Quiet week. Nothing broke. That's yours, partly.   #warm
? endgame tier>=friend
- Your page in my list has a new note. One word. You don't get to read it.   #warm

== life
? endgame beat:calder.3
- Fenn stayed on one ship for twenty years. I asked why. "It knew me." Took me a while.   #warm

== feel
? endgame
- Pleased. Don't spread it about.   #funny

== near
? endgame act:work
- Coil two's at eighty-four. You heard it before I said it. Good.

== bye
? endgame
- Right. Tomorrow's board will look like today's. That's the point of it.
